id: pm-mp49
title: "pm-governance-audit dedupe-audit rejects --status all, breaking explicit all-lifecycle duplicate sweeps"
description: Make the package-owned dedupe-audit command honor the same lifecycle-status filter contract as core list/search so agents can request duplicate analysis across every terminal and active status explicitly.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:contracts","area:extensions",governance-audit
created_at: "2026-07-13T21:36:43.027Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T10:03:22.988Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T04:15:16.664Z"
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "dedupe-audit accepts --status all as an explicit no-restriction sentinel; output echoes filters.status=all; configured custom statuses still validate; omission and --status all return the same all-item candidate set; help, package contracts, completions, docs, and focused tests stay aligned"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: Installed pm-governance-audit with pm 2026.7.13
repro_steps: Run pm dedupe-audit --mode title_exact --status all --limit 10000 --json.
resolution: Governance dedupe audit now treats explicit all as the unfiltered lifecycle selection.
expected_result: pm dedupe-audit --status all succeeds and considers the same items as an omitted status filter.
actual_result: Parser and list execution accept all; unit and packed installed-consumer tests prove explicit and omitted all-status parity.
component: pm-governance-audit/dedupe-audit
customer_impact: Agents cannot express the repository-required all-status duplicate sweep through the audit command and must know that omitting the filter has undocumented broader semantics.
